-- Broadcasting Act 1994, First Schedule: WHICH TEXT governs, for conduct on one day, read on another.
--
-- FORWARD-LOOKING ROW, TARGET unstable.  Not the answer of record.  Needs a build that has the time built-ins
-- (`RULES EFFECTIVE DATE`, TODAY under `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME`, `EVAL UNDER VALID TIME`).
--
-- THE DESIGN (the one chosen; the alternatives, and why not, are in findings/ and NOTES.md):
--   conduct day  D  = the VALID-TIME axis; `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` falls back to it (the presumption against
--                     retroactivity) unless a caller pins the rule-effective axis itself;
--   reading day  R  = the SYSTEM-TIME axis, read with TODAY;
--   a version of the text carries BOTH of its own dates: the day it is deemed to operate from (compared with
--   `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE`) and the day it became visible to a reader (compared with TODAY).
-- The two helper rules below are the ONLY places this row reads an axis directly.  They are named rules, never a
-- bare `TODAY` or `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` handed to a constructor: a bare one escapes the pin (finding 8).
--
-- Everything here is evaluated under whatever the CALLER pinned.  A caller that pins nothing reads the wall
-- clock (finding 6); a caller that pins only the system time makes `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` equal the reading
-- day (finding 2).  The pinned wrappers are in sgbau-act.l4.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgbau-nouns`
IMPORT `sgbau-sched-three-items`
IMPORT `sgbau-sched-s549`

-- Singapore is east of UTC, so the date a system-time pin produces is the date that was pinned (finding 4).
TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

§ `The first deposited edition`

-- The legislative history lists the 2003 Revised Edition as operating from 31 July 2003.
-- Conduct before that day, or a reader before that day, is outside what this row has the text of.
-- src:4602 | 15. 2003 Revised Edition — Broadcasting Act (Chapter 28)
-- src:4604 | Operation : 31 July 2003
@ref Broadcasting Act 1994, Legislative History, entry 15 (src:4602-4604)
`the first deposited edition operated from` MEANS Date 31 7 2003

§ `The date the Legislative History gives S 549/2012`

-- A second witness for the notification's commencement; the tests assert it agrees with sgbau-sched-s549.l4.
-- src:4645 | 20. G.N. No. S 549/2012 — Broadcasting Act (Amendment of First Schedule)
-- src:4646 | Notification 2012
-- src:4648 | Commencement : 1 January 2011
@ref Broadcasting Act 1994, Legislative History, entry 20 (src:4645-4648)
`the Legislative History gives S 549/2012 a commencement of` MEANS Date 1 1 2011

§ `The two days the question turns on`

-- MACHINERY, not text: which axis carries which day.
-- The day whose text governs: the rule-effective axis, which falls back to the valid-time axis (the conduct day).
`the day whose text governs` MEANS `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE`

-- The day the law is being read: the system-time axis.
`the day the law is read` MEANS TODAY

§ `Which version of the First Schedule governs`

-- The three-item text governs unless S 549/2012 applies.
-- S 549/2012 applies to conduct on or after the day it is deemed to have come into operation (1 January 2011),
-- but only to a reader on or after the day it was first published (31 October 2012): before that, no reader
-- could have known of it.  Both limbs are needed; neither is implied by the other.
-- Outside the sources (before the first deposited edition) it REFUSES; it never answers FALSE.
@ref S 549/2012, cl 1 and cl 2; Broadcasting Act 1994, Legislative History, entry 20 (src:4645-4648); the two REFUSE arms rest on entry 15, quoted above
`the version of the First Schedule that governs` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the day whose text governs` BELOW `the first deposited edition operated from`
           THEN REFUSE "not covered: the conduct day is before the first deposited edition (31 July 2003)"
           IF `the day the law is read` BELOW `the first deposited edition operated from`
           THEN REFUSE "not covered: the reading day is before the first deposited edition (31 July 2003)"
           IF     `the day whose text governs` AT LEAST `S 549/2012 is deemed to have come into operation on`
              AND `the day the law is read` AT LEAST `S 549/2012 was first published in the Gazette on`
           THEN `the First Schedule of the TVRO system only`
           OTHERWISE `the First Schedule of three items`

§ `Is the apparatus specified in the First Schedule`

-- The Schedule that governs is asked, and no other.
@ref Broadcasting Act 1994, s 2(1) "broadcasting apparatus", "specified in the First Schedule"
GIVEN apparatus IS AN Apparatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`apparatus is specified in the First Schedule that governs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the version of the First Schedule that governs`
    WHEN `the First Schedule of three items`            THEN `the three-item Schedule specifies the apparatus` apparatus
    WHEN `the First Schedule of the TVRO system only`   THEN `the TVRO-only Schedule specifies the apparatus` apparatus
